WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.880
 Here's a word.

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.920
And you're not going
to like this word--

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:06.820
failure.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.060
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:10.260
Now here's the hitch.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:14.670
It's OK to fail,
to feel insecure.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.830
Now composers are
arrogant, especially when

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.690
we're talking about our music.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.670
But the fact is, the
arrogance is generally

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.950
hiding great insecurity.

00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:24.420
You have to let your ego go.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.090
If you're smart, you're
really doing more listening

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:27.870
than talking.

00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:29.670
You really aren't in charge.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.210
The director's in charge.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:37.310
Your job is to translate their
feelings about their movie

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:38.557
into music.

00:00:38.557 --> 00:00:39.140
One more time.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.096
Hearing the downbeat-- bomm.

00:00:41.096 --> 00:00:44.477
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.630
In the course of
this MasterClass,

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.380
we're going to talk
about instrumentation.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.047
We're going to talk
about orchestration.

00:00:51.047 --> 00:00:52.590
We're going to
talk about melody.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:54.090
We're going to talk
about the tone.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:56.760
The most important thing you're
going to capture in a film

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.850
score is going to be the tone.

00:00:58.850 --> 00:01:01.670
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:02.780
"The Unknown Known"--

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:05.720
I tried to find a
very simple leitmotif.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.810
Guitar-- there's
a mystery to it.

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:13.010
Ostinato begins, B section, and
it ends in a classical da da da

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:16.360
da da.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:20.650
After a hundred and something films,
I'm constantly insecure.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:24.040
Doubting yourself, finding
confidence and moving forward,

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.050
and then doubting what
you've just done--

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:28.805
I think this is the
life of a composer.

00:01:28.805 --> 00:01:30.430
And I think it's the
life of an artist.

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:33.150
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.750
If you're really
going to succeed,

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:37.680
there's no other way but
by doing, making mistakes,

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.410
and then learning from those
mistakes and moving on.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.390
If you take the time
and you learn it,

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.510
I promise you it'll
serve you well.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:50.130
I'm Danny Elfman and
this is my MasterClass.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.480
[MUSIC PLAYING]

